Worker change for the larger model's weights as an external data file (ci/lab/patches/worker-external-data.patch)

Against vendor/rec-worker.js on main at build 8 (8037aec). Apply with: git apply ci/lab/patches/worker-external-data.patch
It needs the new file, published on pub/model-bioclip2-l14-b at add8cf58 (vision.graph.onnx, 2,175,801 bytes, and
vision.weights.bin in four parts, 307,658,752 bytes, with parts.json; made by ci/lab/mem_pub.sh from the shipped
vision.int8.onnx with onnx.save_model(save_as_external_data=True), every tensor unchanged), and a change in the page
(src/cam.rec.js) that is not in this patch: fetch vision.graph.onnx and the parts of vision.weights.bin, check them
against parts.json, and send init with model = the graph's bytes, weights = the joined weights, weightsName =
'vision.weights.bin' (transfer both buffers). With no m.weights the worker behaves exactly as before.

Measured on one GitHub ubuntu-latest machine (lab run 34, runs/lab/34-mem-pub on the ci branch; onnxruntime-web 1.30.0
WASM, one thread, the worker's options; 24 test photos; table by tools/lab/mem_table.py, all runs in ci/lab/mem/results.json):
  headless Chromium, the page's own worker:
    shipped file:        WASM heap 820.9 MiB; renderer peak 1330 MiB while the session is created, 1218 and 1224 MiB
                         during photos 1 and 10; 5.9 s to ready; 4.53 s a photo
    external data form:  WASM heap 429.0 MiB; renderer peak 953 MiB while the session is created, 857 and 864 MiB
                         during photos 1 and 10; 5.8 s to ready; 4.47 s a photo (this patch applied on the machine)
  Node (tools/lab/mem_node.mjs), the file's bytes let go once the session exists:
    shipped file:        WASM heap 819.4 MiB; peak resident 1246 MiB; 4.50 s a photo
    external data form:  WASM heap 429.0 MiB; peak resident 834 MiB; 4.54 s a photo
  vectors: the external data form's are identical to the shipped file's (Node: largest absolute difference 0.0;
  Chromium: cosine 1.000000000 on all 24 photos)

